WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.900
You’ve got plans every evening.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.280
You’re exhausted.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.340
And you remember thinking, “I felt like this
before… what actually helped?”

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.960
For some people, the days before a period

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.220
can bring changes in energy, mood, and
concentration.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.820
But remembering the details takes effort.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.680
When you’re already overwhelmed, another
form to fill

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.580
out can feel like one more task.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.960
Threadline keeps the words you choose to

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.400
save, with your permission and their source.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.560
Ask, “What helped me feel less rushed last
time?”

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.259
Your note says: leaving an evening free.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.040
Then it helps you act.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.040
Our prototype checks a demo calendar,
proposes a break, catches

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.040
a new conflict, and only books after you
approve.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.460
That’s what makes this approach personal:
your own recorded

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.400
words, your saved preferences, and practical
support you control.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.000
This is a fictional example, not a judgment
about how you feel.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.960
A little more breathing room.
